#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid "{ph0}The industrial shift{ph1}"
msgstr "{ph0}Industrijski pomak{ph1}"

#. {ph0}: <a href="#possibilities">
#. {ph1}: </a>
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:293
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid "{ph0}What becomes possible{ph1}"
msgstr "{ph0}Što postaje moguće{ph1}"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:298
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid "What changed in August 2026"
msgstr "Što se promijenilo u kolovozu 2026."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:299
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"Before this work, I had done a lot of manual reverse engineering. I would "
"inspect a function until I had an explanation, then test that explanation "
"against the program. Getting further meant spending more of my own time on "
"the next function. It also meant keeping an increasingly large picture in my"
" head."
msgstr ""
"Prije ovog rada puno sam se bavio ručnim obrnutim inženjeringom. Proučavao "
"bih funkciju dok ne bih dobio objašnjenje, a zatim to objašnjenje "
"provjeravao na programu. Napredovati je značilo trošiti sve više vlastitog "
"vremena na sljedeću funkciju. Značilo je i da u glavi moram držati sve veću "
"sliku cjeline."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:306
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"Most of my RE work is on games. I reconstruct them so their behavior can be "
"understood and eventually carried into a port or a mod. That is the "
"experience behind this article. The method can be useful elsewhere, but each"
" field needs to establish what it can check against a reliable reference."
msgstr ""
"Većina mog RE rada odnosi se na igre. Rekonstruiram ih kako bi se njihovo "
"ponašanje moglo razumjeti i na kraju prenijeti u port ili mod. To je "
"iskustvo iza ovog članka. Metoda može biti korisna i drugdje, ali svako "
"područje mora samo utvrditi što može provjeriti prema pouzdanoj referenci."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:313
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"In August 2026, I started exploring agent-driven RE seriously. I wanted to "
"see how far an agent could get with access to the program and ordinary "
"development tools. Touhou reconstruction gave me a substantial project in "
"which to find out."
msgstr ""
"U kolovozu 2026. počeo sam ozbiljno istraživati RE vođen agentima. Htio sam "
"vidjeti dokle agent može doći ako ima pristup programu i uobičajenim "
"razvojnim alatima. Rekonstrukcija igara Touhou dala mi je opsežan projekt na"
" kojem sam to mogao saznati."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:319
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The early progress was startling. An investigation could keep moving without"
" me choosing every individual step. A failed comparison might send the agent"
" to another caller. It could write a small diagnostic and use the result to "
"decide what to try next. Giving it that freedom made a difference: I could "
"spend more attention on the project's direction and on whether its checks "
"were trustworthy."
msgstr ""
"Rani napredak bio je zapanjujući. Istraživanje je moglo napredovati a da ja "
"ne biram svaki pojedini korak. Neuspjela usporedba mogla je agenta uputiti "
"na drugog pozivatelja. Mogao je napisati malu dijagnostiku i na temelju "
"rezultata odlučiti što će sljedeće isprobati. Ta sloboda napravila je "
"razliku: mogao sam više pažnje posvetiti smjeru projekta i pitanju jesu li "
"njegove provjere pouzdane."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:328
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The pace got my attention first. Then I began wondering what would survive "
"beyond the current project. Would the next game benefit from everything we "
"had just learned?"
msgstr ""
"Prvo me zaokupila brzina. Zatim sam se počeo pitati što će preživjeti izvan "
"trenutnog projekta. Bi li sljedeća igra imala koristi od svega što smo "
"upravo naučili?"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:335
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid "TH08: building on human work"
msgstr "TH08: nadogradnja na ljudski rad"

#. {ph0}: <a href="https://github.com/N0zoM1z0/th08">
#. {ph1}: </a>
#. {ph2}: <a href="https://github.com/GensokyoClub/th08" >
#. {ph3}: </a >
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:336
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"{ph0}TH08{ph1}, Imperishable Night, began as a continuation of "
"{ph2}GensokyoClub's reconstruction{ph3}. Their public source gave me a "
"substantial foundation. It came with knowledge of the build and a history of"
" contributions that I preserved in the continuation."
msgstr ""
"{ph0}TH08{ph1}, Imperishable Night, započeo je kao nastavak "
"{ph2}rekonstrukcije koju je napravio GensokyoClub{ph3}. Njihov javni izvorni"
" kod dao mi je solidnu osnovu. S njime su dolazili znanje o izgradnji "
"programa i povijest doprinosa, koju sam sačuvao u nastavku."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:345
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The imported history ends at the public 10 August checkpoint. My independent"
" continuation began on 13 August. By 19 August, the ledger recorded source "
"for all 1,107 identified game functions."
msgstr ""
"Uvezena povijest završava na javnoj kontrolnoj točki od 10. kolovoza. Moj "
"samostalni nastavak započeo je 13. kolovoza. Do 19. kolovoza registar je "
"bilježio izvorni kod za svih 1.107 prepoznatih funkcija igre."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:350
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"A playable Linux reconstruction port was committed on 24 August, roughly "
"eleven days after the continuation began. A Web edition followed. The native"
" Linux 64-bit release arrived on 30 August."
msgstr ""
"Port rekonstrukcije za Linux u kojem se već moglo igrati predan je u "
"repozitorij 24. kolovoza, otprilike jedanaest dana nakon početka nastavka. "
"Uslijedilo je web izdanje. Nativno 64-bitno izdanje za Linux stiglo je 30. "
"kolovoza."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:355
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"What struck me was that the work had reached a program people could run. "
"Getting there required following problems beyond an individual function. "
"Even when two functions looked correct in isolation, they could accidentally"
" use separate copies of state that should have been shared."
msgstr ""
"Ono što me se dojmilo bilo je to da je rad dosegnuo program koji ljudi mogu "
"pokrenuti. Za to je trebalo pratiti probleme izvan granica pojedine "
"funkcije. Čak i kad su dvije funkcije zasebno izgledale ispravno, mogle su "
"slučajno koristiti zasebne kopije stanja koje je trebalo biti zajedničko."

#. {ph0}: <strong>
#. {ph1}: </strong>
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:362
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"This made reference checks central to the work. I call them "
"{ph0}oracles{ph1}. A code comparison can tell us whether a reconstructed "
"function reproduces the original instructions. A runtime check can tell us "
"whether an exercised route reaches the expected state. The agent proposes an"
" explanation and tests it; a mismatch gives it something specific to "
"investigate."
msgstr ""
"Zbog toga su provjere prema referenci postale središnji dio rada. Zovem ih "
"{ph0}orakulima{ph1}. Usporedba koda može nam reći reproducira li "
"rekonstruirana funkcija izvorne instrukcije. Provjera u vrijeme izvođenja "
"može nam reći dolazi li isprobani put do očekivanog stanja. Agent predlaže "
"objašnjenje i testira ga; nepodudaranje mu daje nešto konkretno za "
"istraživanje."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:370
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid "An exact match with the wrong constant"
msgstr "Točno podudaranje s pogrešnom konstantom"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:371
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"An oracle is software someone wrote. TH08 gave me a clear reminder of how "
"much can depend on that software."
msgstr ""
"Orakul je softver koji je netko napisao. TH08 me jasno podsjetio koliko toga"
" može ovisiti o tom softveru."

#. {ph0}: <code>0.0</code>
#. {ph1}: <code>128.0</code>
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:375
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"In September, a bug reported by a downstream Switch port led back to item "
"auto-collection. The reconstructed source checked player power against "
"{ph0}. The original used {ph1}, the maximum-power threshold."
msgstr ""
"U rujnu je greška koju je prijavio nizvodni port za Switch dovela natrag do "
"automatskog skupljanja predmeta. Rekonstruirani izvorni kod provjeravao je "
"snagu igrača u odnosu na {ph0}. Original je koristio {ph1}, prag maksimalne "
"snage."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:381
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"Normal power is non-negative, so the reconstructed power check was "
"effectively always satisfied. Above the collection line, the game could "
"attract items without requiring maximum power. The other exceptions in the "
"condition were correct. This one constant changed the behavior."
msgstr ""
"Normalna snaga nije negativna, pa je rekonstruirana provjera snage zapravo "
"uvijek bila zadovoljena. Iznad linije skupljanja igra je mogla privlačiti "
"predmete bez zahtijevanja maksimalne snage. Ostali izuzeci u uvjetu bili su "
"ispravni. Ta jedna konstanta promijenila je ponašanje."

#. {ph0}: <strong >
#. {ph1}: </strong >
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:388
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid "{ph0}Yet the function had already passed the exact comparison.{ph1}"
msgstr "{ph0}Ipak, funkcija je već prošla točnu usporedbu.{ph1}"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:394
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"A rebuild can put a constant at a different address. The comparison tool "
"accounted for that by adjusting addresses in the compiled instructions "
"before comparing them with the original. But it never checked the floating-"
"point value stored at the referenced address."
msgstr ""
"Ponovna izgradnja može smjestiti konstantu na drugu adresu. Alat za "
"usporedbu to je uzimao u obzir tako da je prije usporedbe s originalom "
"prilagođavao adrese u kompiliranim instrukcijama. No nikada nije provjeravao"
" vrijednost s pomičnim zarezom pohranjenu na referenciranoj adresi."

#. {ph0}: <code>128.0</code>
#. {ph1}: <code>0.0</code>
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:401
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"That left a hole in the check. It could point the reconstructed instruction "
"at the original's {ph0} while the source still said {ph1}. The instruction "
"bytes matched. The source meant something different."
msgstr ""
"Tako je u provjeri ostala rupa. Rekonstruirana instrukcija mogla je "
"upućivati na {ph0} iz originala, dok je u izvornom kodu i dalje pisalo "
"{ph1}. Bajtovi instrukcije podudarali su se. Izvorni kod značio je nešto "
"drugo."

#. {ph0}: <a href="https://github.com/N0zoM1z0/th08/pull/11" >
#. {ph1}: </a >
#. {ph2}: <a href="https://github.com/N0zoM1z0/th08/pull/13">
#. {ph3}: </a>
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:407
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The {ph0}2 September fix{ph1} corrected the source and made the comparison "
"check the referenced constant's actual bytes. A {ph2}wider audit{ph3} then "
"examined 1,548 floating-literal references. It found another twelve "
"incorrect references across five accepted functions."
msgstr ""
"{ph0}Ispravak od 2. rujna{ph1} popravio je izvorni kod i natjerao usporedbu "
"da provjerava stvarne bajtove referencirane konstante. {ph2}Širi "
"pregled{ph3} zatim je ispitao 1.548 referenci na literale s pomičnim "
"zarezom. Pronašao je još dvanaest pogrešnih referenci u pet prihvaćenih "
"funkcija."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:418
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The comparison now checks every such floating literal. Its tests include "
"deliberately wrong values to make sure they are rejected. We also had to "
"revisit results that had passed the weaker check."
msgstr ""
"Usporedba sada provjerava svaki takav literal s pomičnim zarezom. Njezini "
"testovi uključuju namjerno pogrešne vrijednosti kako bi se osiguralo da se "
"odbiju. Morali smo ponovno pregledati i rezultate koji su prošli slabiju "
"provjeru."

#. {ph0}: <strong>
#. {ph1}: </strong>
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:423
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"{ph0}The oracle needed reconstructing too.{ph1} Repairing it was part of "
"repairing the game."
msgstr ""
"{ph0}I orakul je trebalo rekonstruirati.{ph1} Popravak orakula bio je dio "
"popravka igre."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:427
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"That matters when the team is mostly one person working with agents. I "
"cannot personally inspect every line they produce, so much of my confidence "
"rests on their checks. A shared oracle's blind spot can affect many "
"investigations before I notice it. I have to understand what the checker "
"actually verifies and test it against cases that ought to fail."
msgstr ""
"To je važno kad se tim uglavnom sastoji od jedne osobe koja radi s agentima."
" Ne mogu osobno pregledati svaki redak koji proizvedu, pa se velik dio mog "
"povjerenja temelji na njihovim provjerama. Slijepa točka zajedničkog orakula"
" može utjecati na mnoga istraživanja prije nego što je primijetim. Moram "
"razumjeti što provjeravač zapravo provjerava i testirati ga na slučajevima "
"koji bi morali biti odbijeni."

#. {ph0}: <strong >
#. {ph1}: </strong >
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:435
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"As the work continued, those checks became part of the repository. So did "
"the reasons for source changes and notes that let a later session pick up "
"where an earlier one stopped. {ph0}The repository was becoming the project's"
" working memory.{ph1}"
msgstr ""
"Kako je rad napredovao, te su provjere postale dio repozitorija. Isto "
"vrijedi za razloge promjena izvornog koda i za bilješke koje omogućuju da "
"kasnija sesija nastavi ondje gdje je prethodna stala. {ph0}Repozitorij je "
"postajao radna memorija projekta.{ph1}"

#. {ph0}: <strong >
#. {ph1}: </strong >
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:444
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"{ph0}A successful batch gave us both recovered code and a better environment"
" for the next batch.{ph1}"
msgstr ""
"{ph0}Uspješna serija donijela nam je i rekonstruirani kod i bolje okruženje "
"za sljedeću seriju.{ph1}"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:452
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid "Two different ideas of reconstruction"
msgstr "Dvije različite zamisli o rekonstrukciji"

#. {ph0}: <a
#. href="https://web.archive.org/web/20260909051514/https://github.com/GensokyoClub/th08#important-
#. notice" >
#. {ph1}: </a >
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:453
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"GensokyoClub's {ph0}public README{ph1} makes its disagreement with this kind"
" of work explicit. The notice announces that further development will happen"
" privately until completion. One passage reads:"
msgstr ""
"{ph0}Javni README{ph1} projekta GensokyoClub izričito iznosi neslaganje s "
"ovakvom vrstom rada. Obavijest najavljuje da će se daljnji razvoj odvijati "
"privatno do završetka. Jedan odlomak glasi:"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:464
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The rise of grifters (AI decompilations and ports) in this space taking from"
" our work paints a bad image for future decompilation efforts…"
msgstr ""
"Porast prevaranata (AI dekompilacija i portova) u ovom području, koji "
"uzimaju iz našeg rada, stvara loš dojam o budućim naporima dekompilacije…"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:470
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The notice also describes the psychological toll on the maintainers. Their "
"contribution policy excludes pull requests produced primarily with AI. They "
"have put their free time into difficult work, and that work helped make my "
"continuation possible. I respect the effort behind it. The disagreement I "
"want to discuss is about how reconstruction should proceed and how a "
"contribution should be judged."
msgstr ""
"Obavijest opisuje i psihičku cijenu koju plaćaju održavatelji. Njihova "
"pravila o doprinosima isključuju pull requestove koje je pretežno izradila "
"umjetna inteligencija. Uložili su svoje slobodno vrijeme u težak posao, a "
"taj je posao pomogao da moj nastavak postane moguć. Poštujem trud koji stoji"
" iza njega. Neslaganje o kojem želim govoriti odnosi se na to kako bi "
"rekonstrukcija trebala teći i kako bi se doprinos trebao ocjenjivati."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:479
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"In the manual workflow I knew, developing an understanding of a function and"
" reconstructing it usually fell to the same person. A project relied heavily"
" on that person's expertise. Trust in the contributor mattered because so "
"much of the reasoning happened while they worked."
msgstr ""
"U ručnom tijeku rada koji sam poznavao, razumijevanje funkcije i njezina "
"rekonstrukcija obično su bili zadatak iste osobe. Projekt se uvelike "
"oslanjao na stručnost te osobe. Povjerenje u suradnika bilo je važno jer se "
"velik dio zaključivanja odvijao tijekom njegova rada."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:486
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"Existing projects already preserve knowledge in their source and build "
"tools. What changed for me was that an agent could use that knowledge to "
"pursue the next investigation on its own."
msgstr ""
"Postojeći projekti već čuvaju znanje u svom izvornom kodu i alatima za "
"izgradnju. Za mene se promijenilo to što je agent mogao iskoristiti to "
"znanje da samostalno provede sljedeće istraživanje."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:491
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"In my continuation, I decide the objective and the standard for accepting a "
"result. The agent has broad freedom to investigate. Its proposed "
"reconstruction then has to survive the relevant checks. I want another "
"person to be able to examine why we chose an implementation, even if an "
"agent did most of the work."
msgstr ""
"U svom nastavku ja odlučujem o cilju i o mjerilu za prihvaćanje rezultata. "
"Agent ima široku slobodu istraživanja. Njegova predložena rekonstrukcija "
"zatim mora proći relevantne provjere. Želim da druga osoba može ispitati "
"zašto smo odabrali neku implementaciju, čak i ako je većinu posla obavio "
"agent."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:498
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"This can be a difficult transition. Years of careful work may become the "
"foundation for a continuation that moves much faster. That raises real "
"questions about credit. It also changes what maintainers need to know before"
" accepting a contribution."
msgstr ""
"To može biti težak prijelaz. Godine pažljivog rada mogu postati temelj za "
"nastavak koji napreduje mnogo brže. To otvara stvarna pitanja o priznavanju "
"zasluga. Također mijenja ono što održavatelji moraju znati prije prihvaćanja"
" doprinosa."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:504
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The industrial analogy helps me think about this. In a craft, much of the "
"process depends on the skill of the person carrying it out. Machinery "
"changes where that skill is needed. Someone still has to design the process "
"and recognize when its output is wrong. Different communities can choose how"
" much of that change they want to take on."
msgstr ""
"Industrijska analogija pomaže mi da razmislim o tome. U zanatu velik dio "
"procesa ovisi o vještini osobe koja ga provodi. Strojevi mijenjaju mjesto na"
" kojem je ta vještina potrebna. Netko i dalje mora osmisliti proces i "
"prepoznati kad je njegov rezultat pogrešan. Različite zajednice mogu "
"odabrati koliko te promjene žele prihvatiti."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:512
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"My choice is to continue openly, with the inherited work credited and its "
"history preserved. I want the new work to be reviewable. That gives us a way"
" to ask how far this approach can go and to learn from what goes wrong along"
" the way."
msgstr ""
"Moj je izbor nastaviti otvoreno, uz navođenje zasluga za naslijeđeni rad i "
"očuvanu povijest. Želim da se novi rad može pregledati. Tako imamo način da "
"se pitamo dokle ovaj pristup može ići i da učimo iz onoga što usput krene po"
" zlu."

#. {ph0}: <a
#. href="https://github.com/GensokyoClub/th08/blob/e874b98e210b3be1ed21c5e03d54b883eac5069c/README.md#important-
#. notice" >
#. {ph1}: </a >
#. {ph2}: <a
#. href="https://github.com/GensokyoClub/th08/blob/f345c7dee07b849f2ff93a0029ab5ede126bf12c/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md"
#. >
#. {ph3}: </a >
#. {ph4}: <a
#. href="https://github.com/N0zoM1z0/th08/blob/d2a00f4acb4a13916e07a00bd13f714961714628/README.md#credits-
#. and-provenance" >
#. {ph5}: </a >
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:518
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"Source: GensokyoClub's {ph0}README notice{ph1}, checked on 10 October 2026, "
"and its {ph2}contribution policy{ph3}. The quotation is a shortened excerpt."
" TH08's {ph4}credits and provenance{ph5} record the continuation boundary."
msgstr ""
"Izvor: {ph0}obavijest u README-u{ph1} projekta GensokyoClub, provjerena 10. "
"listopada 2026., i njegova {ph2}pravila o doprinosima{ph3}. Citat je "
"skraćeni izvadak. {ph4}Zasluge i podrijetlo{ph5} projekta TH08 bilježe "
"granicu nastavka."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:536
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid "TH095: experience starts compounding"
msgstr "TH095: iskustvo se počinje gomilati"

#. {ph0}: <a href="https://github.com/N0zoM1z0/th095">
#. {ph1}: </a>
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:537
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"{ph0}TH095{ph1}, Shoot the Bullet, made the value of that experience much "
"easier to see. Its repository began on 29 August with zero confirmed game "
"functions in the ledger. We still had to learn the game. But we already knew"
" much more about how to begin a reconstruction and how to keep it moving."
msgstr ""
"{ph0}TH095{ph1}, Shoot the Bullet, učinio je vrijednost tog iskustva mnogo "
"lakše vidljivom. Njegov je repozitorij započeo 29. kolovoza s nula "
"potvrđenih funkcija igre u registru. I dalje smo morali upoznati igru. No "
"već smo znali mnogo više o tome kako započeti rekonstrukciju i kako je "
"držati u pokretu."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:545
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"By 7 September, all 697 identified game functions had source. By 8 "
"September, 696 had been accepted as exact comparisons. The whole program "
"linked on 9 September. The Windows i386 reconstruction was marked playable "
"on 10 September, about twelve days after initialization."
msgstr ""
"Do 7. rujna sve 697 prepoznatih funkcija igre imale su izvorni kod. Do 8. "
"rujna 696 ih je prihvaćeno kao točne usporedbe. Cijeli je program uspješno "
"povezan linkerom 9. rujna. Rekonstrukcija za Windows i386 označena je kao "
"igriva 10. rujna, oko dvanaest dana nakon inicijalizacije."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:552
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"I found this more exciting than the first project's speed. A fresh target "
"could benefit from work done on another game. The experience was already "
"present in the tools and in the way the project was organized."
msgstr ""
"Ovo mi je bilo uzbudljivije od brzine prvog projekta. Nova meta mogla je "
"imati koristi od rada obavljenog na drugoj igri. Iskustvo je već bilo "
"prisutno u alatima i u načinu na koji je projekt bio organiziran."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:558
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"For example, TH08 had taught us to pay attention to the assembled program "
"early. If several recovered functions depend on the same state, their "
"isolated comparisons leave an important question open. We need to see them "
"working together. That lesson helped shape how we approached TH095's whole-"
"program build."
msgstr ""
"Na primjer, TH08 nas je naučio da rano obratimo pažnju na sastavljeni "
"program. Ako nekoliko rekonstruiranih funkcija ovisi o istom stanju, njihove"
" izolirane usporedbe ostavljaju važno pitanje otvorenim. Moramo ih vidjeti "
"kako rade zajedno. Ta je lekcija oblikovala naš pristup izgradnji cijelog "
"programa TH095."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:565
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"A lesson that stays in my head is useful while I am there. Once it becomes a"
" check that another session can run, it can keep helping after I have moved "
"on. The next agent can use the result without repeating the investigation "
"that led to it."
msgstr ""
"Lekcija koja ostaje u mojoj glavi korisna je dok sam ja tu. Kad postane "
"provjera koju može pokrenuti druga sesija, može nastaviti pomagati i nakon "
"što sam ja otišao dalje. Sljedeći agent može iskoristiti rezultat bez "
"ponavljanja istraživanja koje je do njega dovelo."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:571
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The floating-literal bug belongs in that memory too. It explains why "
"checking a reference also requires checking the data behind it. Keeping that"
" correction with the code helps later projects avoid inheriting the old "
"check's blind spot."
msgstr ""
"Greška s literalima s pomičnim zarezom također pripada u to pamćenje. "
"Objašnjava zašto provjera reference zahtijeva i provjeru podataka koji stoje"
" iza nje. Čuvanje tog ispravka uz kod pomaže kasnijim projektima da ne "
"naslijede slijepu točku stare provjere."

#. {ph0}: <strong >
#. {ph1}: </strong >
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:577
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"{ph0}The method becomes part of the starting material for the next "
"game.{ph1} We can spend more of the next project's effort on what is "
"actually new about its target."
msgstr ""
"{ph0}Metoda postaje dio polaznog materijala za sljedeću igru.{ph1} Više "
"truda sljedećeg projekta možemo uložiti u ono što je zaista novo na njegovoj"
" meti."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:585
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The same benefit is available to people joining later. They can inspect a "
"decision and rerun its check before continuing the work. They do not have to"
" reconstruct the entire project's history to find out why the source looks "
"the way it does."
msgstr ""
"Ista je korist dostupna i ljudima koji se pridruže kasnije. Mogu pregledati "
"odluku i ponovno pokrenuti njezinu provjeru prije nastavka rada. Ne moraju "
"rekonstruirati povijest cijelog projekta da bi saznali zašto izvorni kod "
"izgleda onako kako izgleda."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:593
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid "TH04: the workflow survives a different architecture"
msgstr "TH04: tijek rada preživljava drugačiju arhitekturu"

#. {ph0}: <a href="https://github.com/N0zoM1z0/th04">
#. {ph1}: </a>
#. {ph2}: <a href="https://github.com/nmlgc/ReC98">
#. {ph3}: </a>
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:594
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"{ph0}TH04{ph1}, Lotus Land Story, took this work into the PC-98 DOS era. The"
" target was now a 16-bit environment with four cooperating programs. "
"Understanding its hardware behavior required different evidence from the "
"Windows games. Existing {ph2}ReC98 work{ph3} gave us valuable knowledge and "
"source material here too."
msgstr ""
"{ph0}TH04{ph1}, Lotus Land Story, odveo je ovaj rad u eru PC-98 DOS-a. Meta "
"je sada bilo 16-bitno okruženje s četiri programa koji surađuju. "
"Razumijevanje njegova ponašanja hardvera zahtijevalo je drukčije dokaze nego"
" igre za Windows. I ovdje su nam postojeći {ph2}rad projekta ReC98{ph3} dali"
" vrijedno znanje i izvorni materijal."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:603
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The DOS reconstruction is now working. In my manual testing, I played "
"complete Normal routes through their endings and checked saves. The current "
"work is a native 64-bit port. Establishing a working DOS version first gives"
" that port a reference."
msgstr ""
"DOS rekonstrukcija sada radi. U ručnom testiranju odigrao sam cijele rute na"
" težini Normal do njihovih završetaka i provjerio spremanja. Trenutni rad je"
" nativni 64-bitni port. Prethodno uspostavljena radna DOS verzija daje tom "
"portu referencu."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:609
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The architecture changed what we needed to investigate. It also changed the "
"compiler and runtime against which we checked our work. But the agent could "
"still follow a question through to a result and let that result guide the "
"next experiment."
msgstr ""
"Arhitektura je promijenila ono što smo trebali istražiti. Promijenila je i "
"kompajler i runtime okruženje prema kojima smo provjeravali svoj rad. Ali "
"agent je i dalje mogao pratiti pitanje do rezultata i dopustiti da taj "
"rezultat vodi sljedeći eksperiment."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:615
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"Consider the transition from gameplay to an ending. We need to know what "
"state carries across that boundary and which program is responsible for it. "
"That is something we can investigate against the DOS product. Once the "
"evidence and checks are available, an agent can work through the question "
"much as it did on a Windows title."
msgstr ""
"Uzmimo prijelaz iz igranja u završnicu. Moramo znati koje se stanje prenosi "
"preko te granice i koji je program za to odgovoran. To možemo istražiti na "
"DOS izdanju. Kad dokazi i provjere postanu dostupni, agent može proći kroz "
"to pitanje otprilike kao i na Windows naslovu."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:623
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"This is why TH04 matters to the argument. A substantial platform change did "
"not force us to start over with a new way of working. The architecture "
"defined the problem; the workflow still gave us a way to solve it."
msgstr ""
"Zato je TH04 važan za ovu argumentaciju. Velika promjena platforme nije nas "
"prisilila da počnemo ispočetka s novim načinom rada. Arhitektura je odredila"
" problem, a tijek rada nam je i dalje davao način da ga riješimo."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:629
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"For the 64-bit port, we can now examine the new implementation against "
"behavior already recovered on DOS. The knowledge from reconstruction gives "
"the port something to build on."
msgstr ""
"Za 64-bitni port sada možemo ispitati novu implementaciju u odnosu na "
"ponašanje koje je već rekonstruirano na DOS-u. Znanje iz rekonstrukcije daje"
" portu na čemu graditi."

#. {ph0}: <a
#. href="https://github.com/N0zoM1z0/th04/blob/bb9faca54e2eb3c0d6c757c75d59ac29d2cd5e93/docs/RE_HANDOFF.md"
#. >
#. {ph1}: </a >
#. {ph2}: <a href="https://github.com/N0zoM1z0/th04/tree/port/modern-64" >
#. {ph3}: </a >
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:634
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"Project state as of 10 October 2026: {ph0}DOS reconstruction and manual "
"testing{ph1} · {ph2}64-bit port{ph3}. The port remains in development."
msgstr ""
"Stanje projekta (10. listopada 2026.): {ph0}DOS rekonstrukcija i ručno "
"testiranje{ph1} · {ph2}64-bitni port{ph3}. Port je još u razvoju."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:647
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid "From exact code to readable code"
msgstr "Od točnog koda do čitljivog koda"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:648
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"Once a reconstruction works, I want someone else to be able to understand "
"it."
msgstr "Kad rekonstrukcija proradi, želim da je netko drugi može razumjeti."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:652
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"To me, assembly and raw offsets can feel like old friends. I realise this is"
" a slightly unusual definition of “readable.” Most people would prefer to "
"follow the game's logic without keeping the executable's memory layout in "
"their head."
msgstr ""
"Meni se asembler i sirovi offseti mogu činiti kao stari prijatelji. Shvaćam "
"da je to pomalo neobična definicija „čitljivog”. Većina ljudi radije bi "
"pratila logiku igre, a da u glavi ne mora držati memorijski raspored izvršne"
" datoteke."

#. {ph0}: <strong>
#. {ph1}: </strong>
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:658
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"That is where {ph0}semantic reconstruction{ph1} comes in. A recovered field "
"may still be known mainly by its offset. We follow how the game uses it "
"until we can explain its role. Then we can give it a meaningful name and a "
"type that fits the evidence. We keep the reasoning with the source so the "
"next person can see where that interpretation came from."
msgstr ""
"Tu na scenu stupa {ph0}semantička rekonstrukcija{ph1}. Rekonstruirano polje "
"i dalje može biti poznato uglavnom po svom offsetu. Pratimo kako ga igra "
"koristi dok ne možemo objasniti njegovu ulogu. Tada mu možemo dati smisleno "
"ime i tip koji odgovara dokazima. Obrazloženje čuvamo uz izvorni kod kako bi"
" sljedeća osoba mogla vidjeti odakle ta interpretacija dolazi."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:666
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"This becomes especially important for a port. An absolute address tells me "
"where something lived in the old executable. It gives a 64-bit "
"implementation little help in deciding which object should own that state. "
"To move the behavior safely, we need to recover the relationship behind the "
"old memory access."
msgstr ""
"Ovo postaje osobito važno za port. Apsolutna adresa govori mi gdje se nešto "
"nalazilo u staroj izvršnoj datoteci. 64-bitnoj implementaciji ona malo "
"pomaže u odlučivanju koji objekt treba posjedovati to stanje. Da bismo "
"ponašanje sigurno prenijeli, moramo rekonstruirati odnos koji stoji iza "
"starog pristupa memoriji."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:673
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid "The order I now use is:"
msgstr "Sada koristim sljedeći redoslijed:"

#. {ph0}: <strong>
#. {ph1}: </strong>
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:675
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"{ph0}Recover an exact baseline.{ph1} Compile the reconstructed pieces with "
"the historical compiler. Compare the relevant code and data with the "
"original executable. Record unresolved differences so the next phase has a "
"clear starting point."
msgstr ""
"{ph0}Uspostavi točnu osnovu.{ph1} Kompajliraj rekonstruirane dijelove "
"povijesnim kompajlerom. Usporedi relevantan kod i podatke s izvornom "
"izvršnom datotekom. Zabilježi neriješene razlike kako bi sljedeća faza imala"
" jasnu polaznu točku."

#. {ph0}: <strong>
#. {ph1}: </strong>
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:682
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"{ph0}Build and play it on the original platform.{ph1} Link those pieces into"
" the real program using the original architecture and compiler. Exercise "
"important gameplay paths. This is where we can find problems with shared "
"state or initialization that an isolated function comparison missed."
msgstr ""
"{ph0}Izgradi ga i igraj na izvornoj platformi.{ph1} Poveži te dijelove u "
"pravi program koristeći izvornu arhitekturu i kompajler. Isprobaj važne "
"putanje igranja. Ovdje možemo pronaći probleme sa zajedničkim stanjem ili "
"inicijalizacijom koje je izolirana usporedba funkcija propustila."

#. {ph0}: <strong >
#. {ph1}: </strong >
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:689
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"{ph0}Reconstruct the semantics against both references.{ph1} Take one "
"coherent part of the game at a time and establish what its recovered source "
"means. Improve its representation while preserving the exact comparisons and"
" the playable historical build."
msgstr ""
"{ph0}Rekonstruiraj semantiku u odnosu na obje reference.{ph1} Uzmi jedan po "
"jedan skladan dio igre i utvrdi što njegov rekonstruirani izvorni kod znači."
" Poboljšaj njegov prikaz, a pritom sačuvaj točne usporedbe i povijesnu "
"verziju koja se može igrati."

#. {ph0}: <strong>
#. {ph1}: </strong>
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:698
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"{ph0}Make the modern port.{ph1} Move the established behavior into the new "
"environment, such as a native 64-bit build. The reconstructed original-"
"platform game remains a reference for comparing how the port behaves."
msgstr ""
"{ph0}Napravi moderni port.{ph1} Prenesi utvrđeno ponašanje u novo okruženje,"
" primjerice u nativnu 64-bitnu izvedbu. Rekonstruirana igra za izvornu "
"platformu ostaje referenca za usporedbu ponašanja porta."

#. {ph0}: <strong>
#. {ph1}: </strong>
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:705
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The playable build from the second stage becomes a {ph0}second oracle{ph1} "
"during the third. The first oracle checks whether our changed source still "
"reproduces the relevant original code and data. The second checks that the "
"reconstructed program still builds and behaves correctly along the paths we "
"exercise."
msgstr ""
"Verzija koja se može igrati iz druge faze u trećoj postaje {ph0}drugi "
"orakul{ph1}. Prvi orakul provjerava reproducira li naš izmijenjeni izvorni "
"kod i dalje relevantni originalni kod i podatke. Drugi provjerava da se "
"rekonstruirani program i dalje gradi i ispravno ponaša na putanjama koje "
"isprobavamo."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:713
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"They catch different mistakes. A type change can alter the generated "
"instructions. An ownership change can leave two parts of the game using "
"different copies of state. Keeping both checks available gives the agent a "
"concrete failure to investigate before carrying a refactor further."
msgstr ""
"Hvataju različite pogreške. Promjena tipa može izmijeniti generirane "
"instrukcije. Promjena vlasništva može dovesti do toga da dva dijela igre "
"koriste različite kopije stanja. Kad su obje provjere dostupne, agent ima "
"konkretan neuspjeh za istraživanje prije nego što refaktoriranje odvede "
"dalje."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:720
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"A name needs evidence of its own. An exact comparison cannot tell us whether"
" a field really means “invulnerability time.” We have to establish that from"
" how the game writes and uses it. If the meaning remains uncertain, a "
"neutral name is more helpful to the next reader than a confident guess."
msgstr ""
"Ime treba vlastite dokaze. Točna usporedba ne može nam reći znači li polje "
"doista „vrijeme neranjivosti”. To moramo utvrditi iz načina na koji ga igra "
"zapisuje i koristi. Ako značenje ostane neizvjesno, neutralno je ime "
"korisnije sljedećem čitatelju nego samouvjereno nagađanje."

#. {ph0}: <a href="https://github.com/N0zoM1z0/touhou-reconstruction-
#. factory/blob/717e1b8560783ed17a39fdf159d30aa16bb307a7/docs/semantic-
#. reconstruction.md" >
#. {ph1}: </a >
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:727
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"We learned this order through the projects. TH08 already had playable ports "
"before some of its later historical-platform audits. That made certain "
"defects harder to see. The {ph0}Factory's current workflow{ph1} puts the "
"original-platform build first, so semantic work can use it as a reference "
"before porting begins."
msgstr ""
"Ovaj smo redoslijed naučili kroz projekte. TH08 je već imao portove koji su "
"se mogli igrati prije nekih kasnijih revizija na povijesnoj platformi. Zbog "
"toga su se određeni nedostaci teže uočavali. {ph0}Trenutni tijek rada "
"projekta Factory{ph1} na prvo mjesto stavlja izgradnju za izvornu platformu,"
" pa je semantički rad može koristiti kao referencu prije početka portiranja."

#. {ph0}: <strong >
#. {ph1}: </strong >
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:738
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"{ph0}Exact reconstruction gives us a reference. Semantic reconstruction "
"makes the recovered knowledge usable.{ph1} A port can then build on both."
msgstr ""
"{ph0}Točna rekonstrukcija daje nam referencu. Semantička rekonstrukcija čini"
" rekonstruirano znanje upotrebljivim.{ph1} Port se zatim može nadovezati na "
"oboje."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:747
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid "What makes this an industrial shift"
msgstr "Što ovo čini industrijskim pomakom"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:748
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"These projects changed where I spent my attention. Once agents could carry "
"much of an investigation forward, improving their working environment became"
" one of the most useful things I could do. A better tool could help with "
"every later function that needed it."
msgstr ""
"Ovi projekti promijenili su ono na što trošim pažnju. Kad su agenti mogli "
"nositi velik dio istraživanja, poboljšanje njihova radnog okruženja postalo "
"je jedna od najkorisnijih stvari koje sam mogao učiniti. Bolji alat mogao je"
" pomoći kod svake kasnije funkcije kojoj je trebao."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:755
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"Autonomy matters here. The useful next step often becomes clear only after a"
" failed experiment. An agent needs enough freedom to follow that result "
"somewhere unexpected. If it has to wait for me to prescribe each step, much "
"of the work remains tied to my attention."
msgstr ""
"Autonomija je ovdje važna. Koristan sljedeći korak često postane jasan tek "
"nakon neuspjelog pokusa. Agentu treba dovoljno slobode da taj rezultat prati"
" i na neočekivana mjesta. Ako mora čekati da mu ja propisujem svaki korak, "
"velik dio posla ostaje vezan uz moju pozornost."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:762
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"I expect the agent to make wrong hypotheses. What matters is whether we can "
"test them and learn from the result. A failed check should help it "
"understand the mistake well enough to try again. I still have to decide "
"whether the accumulated evidence supports a project milestone."
msgstr ""
"Očekujem da će agent postavljati pogrešne hipoteze. Važno je možemo li ih "
"testirati i naučiti iz rezultata. Neuspjela provjera trebala bi mu pomoći da"
" dovoljno dobro shvati pogrešku kako bi pokušao ponovno. I dalje moram "
"odlučiti podupiru li prikupljeni dokazi neku prekretnicu projekta."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:769
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"REA gives the agent access to analysis tools. A question about a function's "
"caller can lead straight into inspecting that caller. The reconstruction "
"project supplies the compiler and its own reference checks. The agent can "
"use those to test the source it proposes and see where its explanation holds"
" up."
msgstr ""
"REA agentu daje pristup alatima za analizu. Pitanje o pozivatelju neke "
"funkcije može izravno dovesti do pregleda tog pozivatelja. Projekt "
"rekonstrukcije osigurava prevoditelj i vlastite referentne provjere. Agent "
"ih može iskoristiti da testira izvorni kod koji predlaže i vidi gdje njegovo"
" objašnjenje opstaje."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:776
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The TH08 bug shows why those checks deserve engineering attention of their "
"own. When the same comparison is used across hundreds of functions, a gap in"
" it can spread much further than a mistake in one implementation. Testing "
"the checker improves the feedback available to all that later work."
msgstr ""
"Greška u TH08 pokazuje zašto te provjere zaslužuju vlastitu inženjersku "
"pozornost. Kada se ista usporedba koristi na stotinama funkcija, propust u "
"njoj može se proširiti mnogo dalje od pogreške u jednoj implementaciji. "
"Testiranje provjeravača poboljšava povratne informacije dostupne za sav "
"kasniji rad."

#. {ph0}: <a
#. href="https://collection.sciencemuseumgroup.org.uk/objects/co51439/watts-
#. steam-engine-indicator" >
#. {ph1}: </a >
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:783
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The industrial analogy has a useful historical example here. Boulton and "
"Watt introduced a {ph0}steam-engine indicator in 1796{ph1} to help adjust "
"engine valves. A recording version traced pressure through the piston "
"stroke. It made the engine's internal behavior available for inspection. Our"
" comparison tools serve a similar purpose: they let us examine what the "
"machinery is doing while we improve it."
msgstr ""
"Industrijska analogija ovdje ima koristan povijesni primjer. Boulton i Watt "
"uveli su {ph0}indikator parnog stroja 1796. godine{ph1} kako bi pomogli pri "
"podešavanju ventila stroja. Verzija sa zapisivanjem ucrtavala je tlak "
"tijekom hoda klipa. Time je unutarnje ponašanje stroja postalo dostupno za "
"pregled. Naši alati za usporedbu imaju sličnu svrhu: omogućuju nam da "
"ispitamo što mehanizam radi dok ga poboljšavamo."

#. {ph0}: <strong >
#. {ph1}: </strong >
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:796
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"{ph0}We are in the early stages of this industrial shift.{ph1} Much of the "
"infrastructure is still immature. Agents can move faster than our checks "
"were designed to support, so the process has to develop alongside them. When"
" we find a defect in a shared tool, we have to repair it and revisit the "
"results it affected. The next project can then inherit a stronger tool."
msgstr ""
"{ph0}Nalazimo se u ranoj fazi ove industrijske promjene.{ph1} Velik dio "
"infrastrukture još je nezreo. Agenti se mogu kretati brže nego što su naše "
"provjere osmišljene podržati, pa se proces mora razvijati zajedno s njima. "
"Kad pronađemo grešku u zajedničkom alatu, moramo je popraviti i ponovno "
"pregledati rezultate na koje je utjecala. Sljedeći projekt tada može "
"naslijediti jači alat."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:806
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"There is also a practical limit to any one conversation. It will end before "
"a large reconstruction is finished. The repository has to make it possible "
"for another session to continue without losing the reason for the last "
"decision."
msgstr ""
"Postoji i praktično ograničenje svakog pojedinog razgovora. On će završiti "
"prije nego što se velika rekonstrukcija dovrši. Repozitorij mora omogućiti "
"drugoj sesiji da nastavi bez gubitka razloga za posljednju odluku."

#. {ph0}: <a href="https://github.com/N0zoM1z0/touhou-reconstruction-factory"
#. >
#. {ph1}: </a >
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:812
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The {ph0}Touhou Reconstruction Factory{ph1} grew out of that need. It gives "
"projects a shared way to carry their checks and lessons forward. Work on one"
" game can improve the starting conditions for another."
msgstr ""
"{ph0}Touhou Reconstruction Factory{ph1} nastala je iz te potrebe. Projektima"
" daje zajednički način da svoje provjere i spoznaje prenose dalje. Rad na "
"jednoj igri može poboljšati početne uvjete za drugu."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:822
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"That is what makes the industrial analogy meaningful to me. Experience "
"starts becoming part of tools that others can use. Improving those tools "
"changes how much the next person—or the next agent—can get done."
msgstr ""
"Zato mi je industrijska analogija smislena. Iskustvo počinje postajati dio "
"alata koje drugi mogu koristiti. Poboljšanje tih alata mijenja koliko "
"sljedeća osoba, ili sljedeći agent, može postići."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:830
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid "The projects we can now consider"
msgstr "Projekti koje sada možemo razmotriti"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:831
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The pace matters because it changes the decision to begin. A game could be "
"fascinating to reverse engineer and still demand more of my own attention "
"than I could realistically give it. Many projects would stay ideas."
msgstr ""
"Tempo je važan jer mijenja odluku o početku. Igra može biti fascinantna za "
"obrnuti inženjering, a ipak zahtijevati više moje pozornosti nego što joj "
"realno mogu posvetiti. Mnogi projekti ostali bi samo ideje."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:837
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"Now I can see a way to keep such a project moving through repeated "
"investigations. Getting a working reconstruction makes a port more "
"practical. Recovering readable semantics makes it easier for someone else to"
" explore a mod. The effort put into understanding the game can keep paying "
"off after the first version runs."
msgstr ""
"Sada vidim način da takav projekt kroz ponovljena istraživanja ostane u "
"pokretu. Radna rekonstrukcija čini portiranje praktičnijim. Vraćanje "
"čitljive semantike olakšava nekome drugome istraživanje modova. Trud uložen "
"u razumijevanje igre može se isplaćivati i nakon što prva verzija proradi."

#. {ph0}: <strong >
#. {ph1}: </strong >
#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:844
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"I now look at an unfamiliar program and ask: {ph0}what access, feedback and "
"accumulated knowledge would let an agent work on this reliably?{ph1}"
msgstr ""
"Sada pogledam nepoznat program i pitam se: {ph0}koji pristup, povratne "
"informacije i nakupljeno znanje omogućili bi agentu da pouzdano radi na "
"ovome?{ph1}"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:851
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"That question makes me consider projects I would previously have left alone."
" Each one can improve the way we approach the next. I want to keep exploring"
" how far that can take us."
msgstr ""
"To me pitanje navodi da razmislim o projektima koji bi inače ostali "
"netaknuti. Svaki od njih može poboljšati način na koji pristupamo sljedećem."
" Želim nastaviti istraživati dokle nas to može odvesti."

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:859
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid "Project milestones and sources"
msgstr "Prekretnice projekta i izvori"

#: website/public/blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html:860
msgctxt "page:blog/touhou-reconstruction/index.html"
msgid ""
"The dates describe recorded project checkpoints, checked against public "
"GitHub history on 10 October 2026. Elapsed time is calendar time between "
"commits. Source presence, exact comparisons, a build and a runtime result "
"each name a different milestone."
msgstr ""
"Datumi opisuju zabilježene kontrolne točke projekta, provjerene prema javnoj"
" povijesti na GitHubu 10. listopada 2026. Proteklo vrijeme je kalendarsko "
"vrijeme između commitova. Prisutnost izvornog koda, točne usporedbe, build i"
" rezultat izvođenja svaki označavaju drugu prekretnicu."

